IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wia-types`
IMPORT `wia-days`
IMPORT `wia-connection`
IMPORT `wia-disconnection`
IMPORT `wia-charges`
IMPORT `wia-goal`

-- Water Industry Act 1991 (UK) — the encoder's tests. Expected values are
-- worked by hand from the Act.

§ `Tests`

-- England and Wales bank holidays in 2026 (Good Friday, 3 April, and
-- Christmas Day are disregarded by s 144(7) itself).
hols MEANS LIST Date 1 1 2026, Date 6 4 2026, Date 4 5 2026, Date 25 5 2026, Date 31 8 2026, Date 28 12 2026

§§ `Goal 1 — connections`

-- Fields: owner or occupier, building, domestic, trunk or non-domestic main,
-- notice served, pipe already laid, pipe-laid notice, conditions
-- counter-notice, conditions satisfied.
GIVEN ld IS A BOOLEAN, pp IS A MAYBE DATE, cc IS A MAYBE DATE, ms IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Connection notice`
`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` ld `pipe notice` pp `conditions` cc `met` ms MEANS
    `Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 2 3 2026, ld, pp, cc, ms

-- The relevant day is 3 March; 14 days beginning with it end on 16 March.
#ASSERT `the duty to connect has arisen for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` NOTHING `met` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the relevant day for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` NOTHING `met` NOTHING) EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` NOTHING `met` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 3 2026)
-- Pipe-laid notice 10 March: relevant day 11 March; 21 days end on 31 March.
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` FALSE `pipe notice` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) `conditions` NOTHING `met` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
-- s 47(3): a counter-notice by 16 March is in time; conditions met on
-- 20 March: relevant day 21 March; 14 days end on 3 April.
#ASSERT `conditions were imposed in time for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) `met` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`conditions were imposed in time for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` (JUST (Date 17 3 2026)) `met` NOTHING))
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) `met` (JUST (Date 20 3 2026))) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 4 2026)
-- A late counter-notice imposes nothing.
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` (JUST (Date 17 3 2026)) `met` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 3 2026)
-- Conditions imposed in time and not yet met: no duty yet.
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) `met` NOTHING))
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) `met` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, Date 2 3 2026, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, Date 2 3 2026, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 2 3 2026, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 2 3 2026, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING))

-- s 48: £25.30 is 50 sums of 50p.
#ASSERT `the interest on my deposit` (`Security deposit` OF 25.30, 2/100, Date 15 1 2026, Date 15 1 2027) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the interest on my deposit` (`Security deposit` OF 25.30, 2/100, Date 15 1 2026, Date 14 1 2027) EQUALS 3

-- s 106(4): received 1 June 2026; 21 days after is 22 June.
#ASSERT `the last day to refuse my sewer connection for` (`Sewer notice` OF Date 1 6 2026, NOTHING) EQUALS Date 22 6 2026
#ASSERT `the refusal was in time for` (`Sewer notice` OF Date 1 6 2026, JUST (Date 22 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the refusal was in time for` (`Sewer notice` OF Date 1 6 2026, JUST (Date 23 6 2026)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the refusal was in time for` (`Sewer notice` OF Date 1 6 2026, NOTHING))

§§ `Goal 2 — disconnection for non-payment`

-- Fields: premises, liable, notice, paid, counter-notice, judgment,
-- settlement breach, cut off on. Notice 2 March 2026: seven days beginning
-- with 3 March end on 9 March; the cut-off can come from 10 March.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of premises`, pd IS A MAYBE DATE, cn IS A MAYBE DATE, jd IS A BOOLEAN, ct IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Non-payment case`
`unpaid at` k `paid` pd `counter` cn `judgment` jd `cut` ct MEANS
    `Non-payment case` OF k, TRUE, Date 2 3 2026, pd, cn, jd, FALSE, ct

#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`cutting off would be an offence for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)))
#ASSERT NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 9 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `cutting off would be an offence for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 9 3 2026))
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `a dwelling that is someone's only or principal home` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `cutting off would be an offence for` (`unpaid at` `a dwelling that is someone's only or principal home` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026))
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `other premises listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` `accommodation for the elderly that is someone's only or principal home`
#ASSERT NOT (`the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A`)
#ASSERT `a limiting device would be an offence for` `a house in multiple occupation that is someone's only or principal home`
#ASSERT NOT (`a limiting device would be an offence for` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A`)
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A payment after the seven days does not end the power (F4).
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 12 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- s 61(2)-(3): a counter-notice by 9 March bars the power, unless a
-- judgment is enforceable.
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) `judgment` TRUE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`Non-payment case` OF `premises not listed in Schedule 4A`, TRUE, Date 2 3 2026, NOTHING, JUST (Date 9 3 2026), FALSE, TRUE, Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`Non-payment case` OF `premises not listed in Schedule 4A`, FALSE, Date 2 3 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Goal 3 — charges`

-- Fields: informed, ceased, next meter reading, new occupier informed, by
-- volume.
-- Told Monday 23 March, left Wednesday 25 March: the second working day after
-- 23 March is 25 March, so in time.
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 23 3 2026), Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS NOTHING
-- Told Tuesday 24 March: late. 24 March + 28 = 21 April, before the 15 May
-- reading.
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 24 3 2026), Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS JUST (Date 21 4 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF NOTHING, Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, JUST (Date 1 5 2026), TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2026)
-- Told Thursday 2 April, left Tuesday 7 April: Good Friday and Easter Monday
-- do not count, so the second working day is 8 April: late. 30 April.
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 2 4 2026), Date 7 4 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 2 4 2026), Date 8 4 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 24 3 2026), Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, FALSE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS NOTHING
-- Told after leaving, on 30 April: 28 May; the 15 May reading comes first.
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 30 4 2026), Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2026)
-- A new occupier's notice before I left does not count.
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF NOTHING, Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, JUST (Date 20 3 2026), TRUE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2026)

-- s 144(5)-(6): served Friday 3 April 2026 (Good Friday): two working days,
-- 7 and 8 April.
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` (`Section 62 notice` OF Date 3 4 2026, Date 5 4 2026) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS Date 8 4 2026
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` (`Section 62 notice` OF Date 3 4 2026, Date 30 4 2026) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS Date 30 4 2026

-- Fields: home, unmeasured, impracticable, unreasonable expense, measured
-- from, first notice, remain consumer, s 144A(7) conditions, my notice or
-- consent, occupation changed.
meter MEANS `Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 15 1 2026), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT `I may require a meter for` meter
#ASSERT `the undertaker must meter me for` meter
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` meter EQUALS JUST (Date 14 1 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (`the undertaker may impose a meter for` meter)
#ASSERT NOT (`the undertaker must meter me for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the undertaker must meter me for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`I may require a meter for` (`Meter case` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `the undertaker may impose a meter for` (`Meter case` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 15 1 2026), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 15 1 2026), FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 31 1 2026), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 29 2 2024), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the undertaker may impose a meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the undertaker may impose a meter for` (`Meter case` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `The top-level goal`

empty MEANS `Water customer case` OF hols, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING
full MEANS `Water customer case` OF hols, JUST (`a notice on 2 March 2026, laid` TRUE `pipe notice` NOTHING `conditions` NOTHING `met` NOTHING), JUST (`Security deposit` OF 25.30, 2/100, Date 15 1 2026, Date 15 1 2027), JUST (`Sewer notice` OF Date 1 6 2026, JUST (Date 22 6 2026)), JUST (`unpaid at` `premises not listed in Schedule 4A` `paid` NOTHING `counter` NOTHING `judgment` FALSE `cut` (Date 10 3 2026)), JUST (`Moving out` OF JUST (Date 24 3 2026), Date 25 3 2026, Date 15 5 2026, NOTHING, TRUE), JUST (`Section 62 notice` OF Date 3 4 2026, Date 5 4 2026), JUST meter

#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` empty)'s `duty to connect has arisen` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` empty)'s `earliest day my water can be cut off` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` empty)'s `last day to revoke my meter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `duty to connect has arisen` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `last day to connect` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 3 2026)
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `interest on my deposit` EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `last day to refuse my sewer connection` EQUALS JUST (Date 22 6 2026)
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `sewer refusal in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `premises protected from disconnection` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `earliest day my water can be cut off` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `water may be cut off on the day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `a limiting device would be an offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `last day I can be charged for after leaving` EQUALS JUST (Date 21 4 2026)
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` EQUALS JUST (Date 8 4 2026)
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `I may require a meter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `the undertaker must meter me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `last day to revoke my meter` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 1 2027)
#ASSERT (`the water customer position for` full)'s `the undertaker may impose a meter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
